(28, 'Principal Full-Stack Developer - OCI IoT Platform', 'Oracle', '**Job Description**\nAs a **Principal Full-Stack Developer** , you will play a key role in designing and delivering the next generation of Oracle Internet of Things (IoT) Platform components on OCI. You will work across\n• *Oracle Autonomous Database** , **Java microservices** , **UI** , and **cloud infrastructure** layers to build scalable, reliable, and high-performing systems.\n• *Qualifications:**\n• *Education**\nBS or MS degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.\n• *Experience**\n4 or more years of software development experience, including 3 or more years in a senior or lead engineering role focused on **database-centric** and **cloud-native** applications.\n• *Core Skills**\n+ **Oracle Database 26ai** : schema design, indexing, partitioning, PL/SQL development, query tuning, and performance optimization\n+ **Java** : strong understanding of design principles, concurrency, and microservices architecture\n+ **Data modeling and storage design** for large-scale distributed and/or IoT systems\n+ **Version control and CI/CD** tools and practices\n+ **Cloud experience** with major platforms (OCI preferred)\n+ **Modern UI development** skills\n+ **Docker and Kubernetes** : containerization and orchestration of Java and database-integrated workloads\n+ **Cloud networking and security fundamentals**\n+ **Strong analytical and troubleshooting skills** across application and database layers.\n• *Preferred Skills**\n+ Experience in the **IoT domain** , especially device telemetry, data ingestion, or digital twin systems\n+ Familiarity with **Java 21** (or later) features\n+ Experience building UIs with **Oracle JET** and **MAUI** aligned with **Redwood UX;
