(112, 'Bridge - Operations Associate', 'Stripe', '<h2>Who we are</h2>\n<h3>About Stripe</h3>\n<p>Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone\'s reach while doing the most important work of your career.</p>\n<p>Bridge, a Stripe company, is a rapidly growing business and the number of developers integrating our APIs is growing quickly. We provide Slack-based support to our developers on a wide range of topics in close partnership with our internal engineering team. We’re a small but mighty team that’s expanding global coverage and is looking to make our first Product Support Specialists hires in Mexico City.</p>\n<h3>About the team</h3>\n<p>In this role, you’ll be working directly with developers integrating Bridge APIs and helping them resolve their issues. You will take ownership of complex, technical user issues and work across teams to resolve them. As part of the team, you’ll have a big impact to grow the Product Support operation and enhance various aspects such as capacity planning and forecasting, operational tools and systems, workflow optimization and automation, metrics and reporting, quality control, and more.</p>\n<h2>What you’ll do</h2>\n<p>Stripe is launching Stripe Delivery Centers - a brand new global team to design, implement and grow Stripe’s operations for the next decade. We are looking for dynamic and curious people that have a passion for solving global user issues, building operations, driving process improvements and want to play a front-line role in building this new operational capability for Stripe and accelerating Stripe’s growth. If you like challenging, scaled problems and are an amazing teammate, we want to hear from you!</p>\n<h3> </h3>\n<h3>Responsibilities</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Analyze and troubleshoot complex technical issues through direct user interaction (Slack) and leveraging your knowledge of API documentation.</li>\n<li>Develop product and platform expertise, working closely with Engineering, Product, and Operations teams to diagnose and resolve user issues.</li>\n<li>Strategically optimize and scale support processes to enhance efficiency and improve the overall user experience, incorporating data-driven insights and metrics.</li>\n<li>Lead continuous improvement initiatives aimed at hitting key performance metrics.</li>\n<li>Create and refine documentation to empower users to resolve issues via self-service, reducing dependency on support teams.</li>\n<li>Constantly challenge the status quo and push for innovation in user support strategies and operational processes. </li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Who you are</h2>\n<p>We\'re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.</p>\n<h3>Minimum requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>1-5 years of experience in a customer support role. </li>\n<li>You have a user first mindset and are energized by the challenge of solving difficult problems.</li>\n<li>You have excellent communication skills, both written and verbally.</li>\n<li>You excel in analytical thinking and problem solving.</li>\n<li>You might have prior experience in customer service or internal/external user facing operations processes, you are an organized, self-starter with passion for finding solutions to our user’s challenges.</li>\n<li>You have a process-oriented mindset and ability to get things done.</li>\n<li>You enjoy working in an in-office environment with strong cross team collaboration and support.</li>\n<li>You are able to prioritize and enjoy working in a quick-moving environment.</li>\n<li>You are humble and have a proven track record for working well across teams and with external partners.</li>\n<li>You\'re willing to periodically work a weekend day for which you will receive a weekday off; 
INSERT IGNORE INTO `Job` (`id`, `title`, `company`, `description`, `tags`, `location`, `remote`, `jobType`, `sourceApi`, `sourceUrl`, `externalId`, `embedding`, `embeddedAt`, `postedAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `category`) VALUES
(113, 'Bridge - Operations Associate, Financial Crimes (AML Investigations)', 'Stripe', 'Who we are\nAt Stripe, our Mexico City office is a vibrant hub focused on reshaping the financial landscape for businesses worldwide. The team emphasizes collaboration, innovation, and excellence, working together to enhance the global economy and increase the GDP of the internet. The culture promotes inclusivity, support, and celebrating shared success while handling large volumes of user support cases globally.\n\nAbout Bridge Operations and the Team\nAs Stripe’s global footprint grows and crypto/stablecoins change how money is transferred, Stripe acquired Bridge to leverage stablecoin infrastructure for global payments. Stablecoins enable faster, cheaper, and more efficient transactions but introduce unique compliance challenges.\n\nThe Bridge Operations team expands Stripe’s operational capabilities to support this evolving space. This role is part of the AML Team within Financial Crimes in Bridge Operations, responsible for monitoring, investigating, and reporting suspicious financial activity.\n\nWhat you’ll do\nYou will investigate financial crimes with a focus on blockchain and crypto-related activity. The role involves working with AML processes, analyzing blockchain transactions, identifying illicit activity, and ensuring compliance through detailed investigations and reporting.\n\nResponsibilities\n\nConduct end-to-end AML investigations involving cryptocurrency, stablecoins, and fiat on/off-ramps\n\nUse blockchain analytics tools (e.g., Chainalysis, TRM Labs, Elliptic) to trace and analyze transactions\n\nPerform open-source intelligence (OSINT) and public records research to identify bad actors\n\nDraft and file Suspicious Activity / Transaction Reports (SARs / STRs)\n\nReview and disposition high-risk transaction monitoring alerts with a focus on crypto typologies\n\nDocument investigative rationale and maintain audit-ready records\n\nEnsure operational excellence and make sound decisions in complex, high-risk scenarios\n\nWho you are\nYou are an investigator with strong experience in financial crimes and blockchain analysis, comfortable working in ambiguous environments. You are detail-oriented, analytical, and capable of handling complex crypto-related investigations while maintaining compliance and accuracy.\n\nMinimum requirements\n\n3+ years of experience in AML, financial crimes, risk, or fraud investigations\n\nAt least 2 years focused on crypto/blockchain-related financial crime\n\nExperience using blockchain analytics tools (Chainalysis, TRM Labs, Elliptic, etc.)\n\nProven ability to draft and file SARs/STRs based on complex investigations\n\nStrong research, writing, and analytical skills with OSINT experience\n\nUnderstanding of financial crime typologies, especially in crypto ecosystems\n\nAbility to analyze and synthesize large datasets (on-chain and off-chain)\n\nStrong English communication skills (written and verbal)\n\nPreferred qualifications\n\nACAMS or similar certification\n\nExperience in compliance within FinTech, VASP, or regulated environments\n\nKnowledge of global stablecoin regulatory frameworks\n\nProficiency in English', '[\"AML\",\"Blockchain\",\"CryptoAnalysis\",\"Investigation\",\"Compliance\",\"OSINT\"]', 'Mexico City', 0, 'Full-time', 'greenhouse', 'https://stripe.com/jobs/search?gh_jid=7456081', '7456081', '[0.007059386,-0.01247322,0.003581267,-0.08680724,-0.012262404,0.0012572637,-0.009450696,0.0041801394,0.0025005608,0.02028169,-0.029993402,0.025062231,-0.016456846,-0.017713377,0.1063385,0.010448094,-0.014554404,-0.0029372824,0.012419427,0.0033417048,-0.021745948,0.005023441,-0.010881211,-0.0020316883,-0.024757857,0.026265636,0.008599291,-0.00426048,0.024773987,0.014329674,0.018600903,0.017888097,0.011549807,0.016677903,-0.0046539875,0.006735043,-0.030285932,-0.029167013,-0.0016539731,0.037950486,0.013439617,0.048326675,-0.052484736,-0.014645711,0.007922923,-0.025435235,-0.005541798,-0.00