(399, 'Regulatory Reporting Program Manager, Stablecoin', 'Stripe', '<h2><strong>Who we are </strong></h2>\n<h3><strong>About Stripe</strong></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;
INSERT IGNORE INTO `Job` (`id`, `title`, `company`, `description`, `tags`, `location`, `remote`, `jobType`, `sourceApi`, `sourceUrl`, `externalId`, `embedding`, `embeddedAt`, `postedAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `category`) VALUES
(400, 'Renewals Specialist', 'Stripe', '<h2><strong>Who we are</strong></h2>\n<h3><strong>About Stripe</strong></h3>\n<p>Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone\'s reach while doing the most important work of your career.</p>\n<h3><strong>About the team</strong></h3>\n<p>The Renewals Team is a specialized strategic function that partners with Stripe’s Global Sales organization to secure and expand revenue. We act as a critical analytical and operational bridge between multiple cross functional partners to ensure a seamless deal lifecycle for our most important users.</p>\n<p>Our team is defined by rigorous thinking, data driven decision making, and a user first approach to complex commercial challenges. As a dedicated partner, we provide the market intelligence and strategic insights necessary to help account teams navigate renewals with accuracy and speed, directly influencing Stripe’s long term growth and product strategy.</p>\n<h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2>\n<p>As a Renewals Specialist, you will partner with Sales, Customer Success, and internal stakeholders to drive revenue retention and expansion. You will collaborate with account teams to develop and present compelling proposals, ensuring large scale contracts are quoted accurately and renewed on schedule. We are seeking a proactive professional who excels in ambiguous, fast growing environments and can solve complex problems with limited oversight.</p>\n<p>The successful candidate will demonstrate a strategic and analytical approach to identifying cross functional challenges and building consensus across the organization to meet aggressive targets. You will be responsible for crafting sophisticated deal structures, managing complex initiatives, and utilizing data to drive informed decision making. Our ideal candidate has a proven ability to design scalable processes and work effectively with internal partners to execute against fluctuating volumes while maintaining a high standard of operational excellence.</p>\n<h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong>:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Work with existing Stripe customers and Stripe Account Executives to develop and execute sales strategies to renew and expand Stripe’s revenue</li>\n<li>Partner on deal strategy and commercial negotiations for large, complex renewals</li>\n<li>Research user data and history and make recommendations based on prior activity</li>\n<li>Audit Sales feedback and user account signals to identify evolving business needs that drive renewal, expansion, and upsell growth.</li>\n<li>Assist with complex quote creation</li>\n<li>Identify and refine scalable workflows to drive operational efficiency through automation, tooling enhancements, and strategic outsourcing where appropriate.</li>\n<li>Cultivate an environment of operational excellence characterized by high individual ownership, ethical integrity, and a collective commitment to a positive team dynamic.</li>\n<li>Report on a regular weekly, monthly, and quarterly cadence to key stakeholders, with a strong analytical approach and crisp communication style.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2>\n<p>We\'re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.</p>\n<h3><strong>Minimum requirements</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>5+ years of experience in high-growth Renewals, Strategic Account Management or Sales, with a proven track record in the SaaS or FinTech sector</li>\n<li>Proven track record in successfully owning and delivering manual and automated processes</li>\n<li>Experience working with Salesforce.com and/or Salesforce CPQ (SteelBrick); 
INSERT IGNORE INTO `Job` (`id`, `title`, `company`, `description`, `tags`, `location`, `remote`, `jobType`, `sourceApi`, `sourceUrl`, `externalId`, `embedding`, `embeddedAt`, `postedAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `category`) VALUES
(401, 'Renewals Specialist', 'Stripe', '<h2><strong>Who we are</strong></h2>\n<h3><strong>About Stripe</strong></h3>\n<p>Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone\'s reach while doing the most important work of your career.</p>\n<h3><strong>About the team</strong></h3>\n<p>The Renewals Team focuses on facilitating contract renewals at Stripe. We partner with sales on the administrative and analytical aspects of a renewal, including identifying upcoming renewals, determining historical consumption and pricing, positioning value, surfacing upsell/cross-sell opportunities and helping close deals.</p>\n<h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2>\n<p>The Renewals Specialist will partner with AE’s, sales management, Customer Success and internal partners to retain and expand user revenue. The successful candidate will work with their sales team to produce and present compelling customer proposals, ensuring that large contracts are renewed on-time and quoted accurately. We are looking for a self-starter to join our team who has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguity, operating in a fast-growing environment, and solving problems with limited oversight. The ideal candidate will demonstrate that they can or have partnered closely with cross-functional teams, deliver tasks, project manage complex initiatives and make data-driven decisions. Our ideal candidates will have had experience crafting and structuring deals, and building scalable processes. </p>\n<p>A successful candidate will have a demonstrated ability to think strategically and analytically to identify cross-functional challenges and build consensus, within team and across functions, to execute against fluctuating volumes and complex projects. </p>\n<h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong>:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Proactively manage Renewal pipelines and activity / engagement milestones</li>\n<li>Research user purchase and renewal history and make recommendations based on prior activity</li>\n<li>Manage KPIs relating to Renewal coverage scope by segment / region </li>\n<li>Gather requirements from Sales and User account signals for renewal, expansion and upsell opportunities</li>\n<li>Assist with complex quote creation to allow Sales to focus on upsell</li>\n<li>Help develop and execute Stripe’s Renewals Desk strategy, in alignment with Stripe’s Sales business strategy</li>\n<li>Identify and optimise repeatable and scalable processes, looking to automate, re-tool, process improve and vendorise as appropriate</li>\n<li>Help cultivate a team culture that includes high ownership, customer-first focus, fast-paced, high integrity, and an optimistic and positive environment</li>\n<li>Report out on a regular weekly, monthly, and quarterly cadence to key stakeholders, with a strong analytical approach and crisp communication style</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2>\n<p>We\'re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.</p>\n<h3><strong>Minimum requirements</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>3+ years of experience in Renewals, Account Management, or Customer Success ideally in a tech environment</li>\n<li>Proven track record in successfully owning and delivering manual and automated processes</li>\n<li>Strong leadership experience, including cultivating high-performance, positive team culture and developing close, cross functional partnerships</li>\n<li>Sound business judgment, strong analytical skills, and a proven track record of taking ownership, leading data-driven analyses, and influencing results</li>\n<li>Experience working within a high-growth, technology company with the ability to operate successfully in a lean, fast-paced organisation</li>\n<li>Highly organised, multi-tasking skills, taking ownership and being efficient in ambiguous situations</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><strong>Preferred qualifications</strong>:</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Lean Six Sigma certification, or proven experience employing the methodology</li>\n<li>Experience working in the financial services/payments industry</li>\n</ul>', '[\"Project Management\",\"Communication\",\"Leadership\",\"Customer Success\"]', 'Dublin', 0, 'Full-time', 'greenhouse', 'https://stripe.com/jobs/search?gh_jid=7635916', '7635916', '[-0.014976925,0.016894324,0.016811257,-0.058400612,-0.006020134,0.0050657745,-0.0006369127,-0.008053431,0.009393448,0.010510493,-0.0073806737,-0.0023349994,-0.026247036,0.006819861,0.107542574,0.013694513,0.018882627,0.0006090967,0.00095052447,0.01053707,-0.0034786423,0.017261177,-0.010115397,0.012609349,-0.0154643925,-0.013864228,0.028924864,0.0031804782,0.014617827,0.0034723785,0.0015929114,0.014612829,0.006113151,-0.005763884,0.00914102,0.003122564,-0.0009326039,0.012568027,-0.012716606,0.019871606,0.0047192215,0.00836436,0.010713972,-0.025814896,-0.026616544,-0.052296694,-0.016053062,-0.02634455,-0.0154729,-0.0052915937,-0.015010359,-0.002322005,-0.011961782,-0.1506041,-0.019722393,-0.012121726,0.0043348996,-0.00808272,0.01851191,-0.01878952,-0.0014587196,0.043649837,-0.012547971,-0.02708528,0.0032682633,0.010059308,-0.01703416,0.007060983,-0.011552936,-0.0019381711,0.009391667,0.01311138,-0.009631794,0.0010830866,-0.0066212015,-0.013199801,0.045045525,0.0020383322,0.0042573456,-0.010459372,0.024506083,0.020668598,-0.024083283,-0.017770361,0.017399328,-0.014421233,0.0063137314,0.008579443,0.005529609,0.0103343,0.0021421388,-0.004467975,0.017849268,0.0041501233,-0.023985561,-0.009118264,-0.0035517507,-0.0052026114,0.026580418,-0.0