INSERT IGNORE INTO `Job` (`id`, `title`, `company`, `description`, `tags`, `location`, `remote`, `jobType`, `sourceApi`, `sourceUrl`, `externalId`, `embedding`, `embeddedAt`, `postedAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `category`) VALUES
(655, 'Manager, Strategic Sales', 'Figma', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you\'re brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you\'re excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!</p></div><p>Figma is looking for a Manager, Strategic Sales to join our dynamic team of creatives, engineers, marketing wizards, and brilliant business folks. You aren’t the typical sales leader, and we aren’t the typical product development company. At Figma, we think outside the box, lift constraints that block our imagination everyday, and we expect you to do the same. With this role you’ll get in at the ground floor in a fast growing sales org. You’ll consult with our existing customer base and potential customers in driving meaningful relationships that add value to the customer experience and revenue to our bottom line.</p>\n<p>Figma is growing and moving fast. Our next team member will have an agile, dynamic mindset, be comfortable embracing change, a true team-player, and love working with our growing footprint of Fortune 1000 customers. You won’t be alone! Figma has an incredible team and you’ll work closely with other groups including Support, Design, Engineering, Product Marketing, Customer Success, and Community. As Manager, Strategic Sales, you will lead a team of Account Executives responsible for continuing the growth of our Enterprise products. You will report directly to our VP of Enterprise and Strategic Sales, North America. </p>\n<p>This is a full time role. Open to remote within the U.S., with a preference for candidates based in one of our hubs.</p>\n<h4><strong>What you’ll do at Figma:</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Lead our Strategic Segment for North America </li>\n<li>Participate in customer and prospect meetings with our largest and most strategic customers</li>\n<li>Attract and retain top talent across the team </li>\n<li>Help shape and further develop sales processes and initiatives</li>\n<li>Establish the strategy for the continued growth across our most strategic segment</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>We\'d love to hear from you if you have:</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>7+ years of sales experience (preferably within SaaS)</li>\n<li>2+ years of management experience</li>\n<li>Understanding of our technical and competitive landscape</li>\n<li>Ability to thrive in a constantly changing and evolving environment</li>\n<li>Exceptional coaching, writing, discovery and presentation skills</li>\n<li>Excitement for increasing customer happiness and developing lasting customer relationships</li>\n<li>Proven track record of leading successful and consistent sales team </li>\n</ul>\n<p>At Figma, one of our values is Grow as you go. We believe in hiring smart, curious people who are excited to learn and develop their skills. If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with the points outlined in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.</p><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;
INSERT IGNORE INTO `Job` (`id`, `title`, `company`, `description`, `tags`, `location`, `remote`, `jobType`, `sourceApi`, `sourceUrl`, `externalId`, `embedding`, `embeddedAt`, `postedAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `category`) VALUES
(656, 'Manager, Web Development', 'Figma', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you\'re brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you\'re excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!</p></div><p>We’re looking for a Manager, Web Development to lead our dedicated team of web developers. In this role, you’ll play a vital role in building and maintaining our web platform. You will collaborate with designers, marketers, data scientists, and engineers to develop and maintain Figma\'s web properties. These include the Figma.com, designsystems.com, and config.figma.com. </p>\n<p>You\'ll work with a variety of modern web technologies including React, NextJS, Typescript, GraphQL, headless CMS (Sanity/Contentful/Payload) and other NodeJS based frameworks. Your role will also include collaborating on planning goals, roadmapping, and managing vendor relationships. </p>\n<p>This is an ideal role for a leader who loves the intersection of design, content, and web and who wants to shape how Figma shows up in the world—with clarity and craft.</p>\n<p>This is a full time role that can be held from one of our US hubs or remotely in the United States.</p>\n<h4>What you’ll do at Figma:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Lead the Web Development team by removing blockers and providing guidance while empowering the team to drive technical decisions across Figma.com, config.figma.com, and designsystems.com</li>\n<li>Hire, manage, support, and develop a team of engineers</li>\n<li>Partner with cross-functional teams to set strategy, priorities, and mission for teams and projects</li>\n<li>Manage complex projects from start to finish—maintaining timelines, collaborator expectations, ticket triaging, and regularly presenting with teammates and leadership</li>\n<li>Collaborate closely with Engineering, Growth, Brand, and SEO teams to ensure reliable, performant, accessible, and secure sites</li>\n<li>Act as a bridge between the marketing web team and our security and infrastructure groups — surfacing needs, sharing context, and facilitating cross-functional improvements through implementation and thorough documentation</li>\n<li>Create and maintain comprehensive testing strategies and make recommendations for the latest web technologies and improvements</li>\n<li>Mentor team members, support new hires during onboarding, and provide technical guidance to technical and non-technical collaborators</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"section page-centered\">\n<h4>We\'d love to hear from you if you have:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>7+ years of full-stack development experience, with deep expertise in TypeScript, React, Next.js, and Node.js, plus hands-on experience with Playwright, Jest, and other E2E testing frameworks</li>\n<li>Strong background in modern web architecture, including headless CMS platforms (Sanity, Contentful, Payload), caching strategies, CDN proxies, edge functions, and performance optimization across SSR and SSG environments</li>\n<li>3+ years of people management experience leading in-house web development teams, providing technical direction, mentorship, and delivery oversight</li>\n<li>Deep knowledge of web best practices spanning security (DDoS, XSS, SQL injection), database management, cloud infrastructure, CI/CD strategy, deployment processes, legal/cookie compliance, performance, and WCAG 2.2 accessibility standards</li>\n<li>Proven ability to lead complex projects and align cross-functional stakeholders across design, product, legal, data, and marketing—facilitating productive discussions and driving teams toward shared outcomes</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>While not required, it’s an added plus if you also have:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience using Figma</li>\n<li>Experience with multi-product brands</li>\n<li>Solid understanding of conversion rate optimization standard methodologies, using A/B testing to achieve results</li>\n<li>Experience working on SEO-driven projects, localization, &amp; 
