(658, 'Office Manager (Tel Aviv, Israel)', 'Figma', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><p>Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you\'re brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you\'re excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!</p></div><div class=\"section page-centered\">\n<div>\n<p>Our Office Manager will be an integral part of the Workplace team and will provide HR support to the Tel Aviv hub. In this hybrid role you’ll manage day-to-day office operations, provide a welcoming experience for employees and guests, and support critical people operations initiatives—from onboarding to benefits to union relations.<br><br>This is a full time in-person role that will be based in our Tel Aviv hub. </p>\n<p><strong>What you\'ll do at Figma:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Be the face of the office by welcoming and assisting guests, vendors and employees upon arrival</li>\n<li>Coordinate logistics and hospitality for in-office meetings, events, and team offsite. Leading planning for events including celebrations, cultural holidays, employee resource group activities (Some may take place out of hours so flexibility is required)</li>\n<li>Ensure Workplace is clean, safe and fully operational each day- including managing &amp; 
