(814, 'Audiovisual Broadcast Engineer, IT Engineering', 'Anthropic', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2>\n<p>As an AV Broadcast Engineer, you\'ll serve as the technical engineering lead ensuring flawless execution of the events and broadcasts that enable communication across our global organization. You\'ll act as both technical director and primary escalation point for complex production challenges, bringing deep expertise in audio DSP, video broadcast systems, and camera technologies to every event—from intimate executive presentations to company-wide all-hands broadcasts reaching thousands of participants.</p>\n<p>This is an opportunity to define what world-class event production looks like at a cutting-edge AI research organization. You\'ll drive the long-term vision for how events and broadcasts evolve for the audiovisual team while working at the intersection of hands-on engineering and strategic infrastructure planning—making real-time technical decisions during live productions while collaborating on the global broadcast standards and systems that scale with our organization. Your work directly enables the collaboration and transparency that advance our AI safety mission.</p>\n<h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>Engineering Lead &amp; 
