(841, 'Copyright Operations Program Manager', 'Anthropic', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2>\n<p>We are seeking a Copyright Operations Program Manager to help build and run Anthropic\'s dedicated Copyright Operations program. This role is critical to standing up the infrastructure, workflows, and processes needed to handle copyright compliance at scale. You\'ll be responsible for processing DMCA and other copyright takedown notices, managing URL opt-out requests, supporting regulatory compliance workflows, and helping consolidate intake channels into a unified, trackable system. This is a ground-floor opportunity: you\'ll be building the program and running it simultaneously, shaping how Anthropic handles copyright operations as our product capabilities and international obligations grow.</p>\n<h2><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Partner with Legal, Engineering, Safeguards, and Support Ops to develop and iterate on copyright operations workflows</li>\n<li>Define and report on operational metrics — volume, resolution times, compliance rates — and use that data to identify gaps and improve processes</li>\n<li>Scale documentation, decision frameworks, and training materials that enable the program to grow beyond individual knowledge</li>\n<li>Identify and drive automation opportunities to reduce manual overhead and improve consistency</li>\n<li>Own end-to-end processing of copyright takedown notices and related policies, from intake through resolution</li>\n<li>Build and maintain specialized intake forms and playbooks as new product capabilities launch</li>\n<li>Support copyright compliance workflows, including transparency documentation and rights reservations </li>\n</ul>\n<h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>You may be a good fit if you have:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>5+ years of experience in copyright operations, content moderation, or a closely related field with demonstrated program-building experience</li>\n<li>Familiarity with DMCA processes, copyright law fundamentals, or intellectual property operations — you don\'t need to be a lawyer, but you should understand the basics of how takedown notices work and why they matter</li>\n<li>Experience building or significantly improving operational workflows — taking something messy or manual and turning it into a repeatable, well-documented process</li>\n<li>Strong project management skills with the ability to manage high-volume, deadline-driven work while also stepping back to design better systems</li>\n<li>Comfort navigating ambiguity and working in fast-moving environments where you\'re often building the playbook as you go</li>\n<li>Attention to detail and sound judgment when assessing whether a notice or request meets defined criteria</li>\n<li>Experience working cross-functionally with Legal, Engineering, or Product teams to drive operational improvements</li>\n<li>Familiarity with international copyright or data regulations (EU AI Act, GDPR) is a plus but not required</li>\n<li>Experience with automation tooling, case management systems, or AI-assisted workflows is a plus</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>The annual compensation range for this role is listed below. </p>\n<p>For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.</p></div><div class=\"title\">Annual Salary:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>€155.000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;
INSERT IGNORE INTO `Job` (`id`, `title`, `company`, `description`, `tags`, `location`, `remote`, `jobType`, `sourceApi`, `sourceUrl`, `externalId`, `embedding`, `embeddedAt`, `postedAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `category`) VALUES
(842, 'Corporate Accountant, Accounting Operations', 'Anthropic', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2>\n<p>We are looking for a Corporate Accountant to join our Corporate Accounting Operations team at Anthropic. You will work as a key preparer across the monthly and quarterly close cycle and work cross-functionally across the organization to solve complex problems on a regular basis. .</p>\n<p>This is an opportunity for someone who thrives in ambiguity, moves quickly without sacrificing accuracy, and genuinely enjoys building better processes — not just maintaining them. If you are looking for an opportunity to make a significant impact on the financial infrastructure of an innovative company, come join us in our mission to build cutting-edge, safe AI.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h2><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Serve as a primary preparer across month-end and quarter-end close activities spanning various corporate accounting areas</li>\n<li>Prepare and own balance sheet reconciliations, journal entries, and flux analysis commentary across your portfolio of accounts, that may include leases, fixed assets, prepaid expenses, accruals, and payroll-related accruals</li>\n<li>Prepare and maintain technical accounting memos, documenting conclusions in accordance with US GAAP and ensuring audit-ready support</li>\n<li>Support and operate within the company’s internal controls framework, with a focus on SOX compliance and control documentation</li>\n<li>Identify repetitive, rules-based accounting tasks and build scalable workflows — including leveraging Claude and other tools — to reduce manual effort and increase accuracy</li>\n<li>Collaborate with Technical Accounting on complex transactions, policy development, and application of new or evolving accounting standards</li>\n<li>Support external audit requests and ensure timely delivery of audit-ready schedules and supporting documentation</li>\n<li>Contribute to system implementations and process improvement initiatives as the team and company continue to scale</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p>\n<h2><strong>You may be a good fit if you:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hold an active CPA license (required)</li>\n<li>Have 7+ years of accounting experience, preferably in startup or high-growth environments with 2+ years of experience in a public company</li>\n<li>Big 4 Audit background</li>\n<li>Have experience operating across multiple accounting functions (e.g., corporate close, lease accounting, payroll accounting) — comfort with breadth is essential</li>\n<li>Can move between preparer-level execution and technical accounting analysis — writing a technical memo and closing your accruals in the same week should feel familiar</li>\n<li>Have experience working in or building out SOX-compliant control environments</li>\n<li>Are a self-starter who identifies what needs to be done and does it without waiting to be asked</li>\n<li>Communicate clearly and directly with non-accounting partners — you can explain a journal entry to non finance stakeholders</li>\n<li>Are comfortable with ambiguity and can make good decisions with incomplete information</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p>\n<h2><strong>Strong candidates may also:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Have experience working in a fast-paced startup environment</li>\n<li>Workday financials experience or ERP implementation</li>\n<li>Have the ability to meet deadlines without sacrificing the quality of your work product</li>\n<li>Be comfortable with handling ambiguity and working with minimal supervision</li>\n<li>Take the initiative to apply their knowledge of processes and systems and recommend well-considered improvements</li>\n<li>Exhibit knowledge of how to implement a change and good instinct in predicting its effects, and knowledge of how to “get it right” the first time</li>\n<li>Bring genuine curiosity about how AI tools can eliminate low-value, repetitive work from accounting workflows</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>The annual compensation range for this role is listed below. </p>\n<p>For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.</p></div><div class=\"title\">Annual Salary:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$160,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;
