o product teams to ensure our offerings meet DOE and national laboratory requirements<br><br></li>\n<li>Take a leadership role in growing our DOE presence while maintaining hands-on engagement with key accounts<br><br></li>\n<li>Collaborate across teams to ensure coordinated delivery of commitments and maintain appropriate documentation of customer engagements<br><br></li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>You may be a good fit if you have:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>7+ years of enterprise sales experience with at least 5 years selling into DOE and/or the national laboratory complex, with a proven track record of driving adoption of emerging technologies<br><br></li>\n<li>Deep understanding of DOE\'s organizational structure, mission areas, and technology modernization priorities<br><br></li>\n<li>Expertise in the national laboratory ecosystem<br><br></li>\n<li>Demonstrated ability to balance strategic leadership with hands-on sales execution<br><br></li>\n<li>Experience navigating DOE procurement processes, including lab-specific contracting mechanisms<br><br></li>\n<li>Strong track record of exceeding revenue targets in the federal civilian or DOE space<br><br></li>\n<li>Excellent relationship-building skills across all levels, from researchers and technical teams to program managers and senior agency leadership<br><br></li>\n<li>Proven ability to coordinate across multiple stakeholders, including cloud providers, M&amp;
