(911, 'European Tax Lead', 'Anthropic', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2>\n<p>We\'re hiring our first dedicated international tax professional in Europe, based in Dublin. You\'ll be a key member of Anthropic\'s tax team, working closely with our Head of International Tax Operations and Business Advisory and reporting into our San Francisco headquarters.</p>\n<p>As European Tax Lead, you\'ll own direct tax compliance and advisory across our European entities (Ireland, UK, Germany, France, Switzerland) and help build tax infrastructure to support Anthropic\'s rapid international expansion.</p>\n<h2><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Lead European direct tax compliance, working with external advisors (KPMG, PwC, Deloitte) to ensure timely and accurate filings across all jurisdictions</li>\n<li>Support transfer pricing documentation and intercompany transactions for European entities, including cost-plus arrangements and IP licensing structures</li>\n<li>Advise on permanent establishment risks, entity structuring, and operational tax considerations as Anthropic expands European commercial activities</li>\n<li>Support EU AI Act-related entity and operational structuring from a tax perspective</li>\n<li>Partner with indirect tax personnel on VAT/GST matters to align on tax strategy and overall compliance requirements.</li>\n<li>Partner with Finance, Legal, and People teams on European payroll taxes, equity compensation, and employee mobility matters</li>\n<li>Build relationships with local tax authorities and manage any inquiries or audits</li>\n<li>Contribute to global tax projects including public company readiness, SOX compliance, and tax technology implementations</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>You may be a good fit if you:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>10–12 years of international tax experience, ideally with a mix of Big 4/advisory and in-house roles</li>\n<li>Strong technical knowledge of Irish corporate tax, EU tax directives, and cross-border tax issues</li>\n<li>Deep experience with transfer pricing documentation, intercompany agreements, and IP planning structures</li>\n<li>Exposure to technology or high-growth company tax matters preferred</li>\n<li>CTA, AITI, or equivalent professional qualification</li>\n<li>Excellent communication skills and ability to work across time zones with US-based colleagues</li>\n<li>Self-starter who thrives in ambiguity and can build processes from the ground up</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Strong candidates may have:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Experience with R&amp;
INSERT IGNORE INTO `Job` (`id`, `title`, `company`, `description`, `tags`, `location`, `remote`, `jobType`, `sourceApi`, `sourceUrl`, `externalId`, `embedding`, `embeddedAt`, `postedAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `category`) VALUES
(912, 'Event Designer', 'Anthropic', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2>\n<p>The Creative Studio is Anthropic’s in-house creative team responsible for the brand expression across Anthropic and Claude. We care about craft, making things by hand and using AI when it makes sense. The team is growing, and we’re looking for people who do excellent work to join us. The stakes are real, and there’s room to shape what all this becomes.</p>\n<p>We are looking for an Event Designer to design and art direct Anthropic\'s presence at physical and digital events. Working closely with the event design team, you will bring our brand to life across industry conferences, hosted events, and executive experiences — ensuring all work we produce in the world feels cohesive, elevated, and unmistakably Anthropic.</p>\n<p>A significant part of this role involves defining how Anthropic presents itself within third-party environments where we appear alongside competitors in a crowded field. This requires strategic thinking about visual differentiation, establishing and maintaining a high creative standard for booth and spatial experiences, and providing clear art direction to external agencies and fabrication vendors to ensure execution meets our expectations.</p>\n<p>This is a hands-on design role that extends well beyond producing booth graphics. We are looking for someone who brings rigor and craft to every surface — from environmental design and presentations to interactive elements and digital touchpoints — and who thinks carefully about how people encounter and move through a space.</p>\n<h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Art direct and execute design across industry conferences, hosted events, and executive experiences — including third-party events where Anthropic appears alongside competitors in a crowded enterprise landscape.</li>\n<li>Establish and uphold the visual and experiential standard for booth environments, with consideration for spatial layout, environmental graphics, materials, lighting, and interactive elements that distinguish our presence.</li>\n<li>Design and think through the full attendee journey — identifying how visitors encounter, enter, and navigate an Anthropic-branded space, and where design can create meaningful and memorable moments.</li>\n<li>Provide creative direction to external agencies, fabricators, and production vendors, maintaining quality and brand integrity across all stages of execution.</li>\n<li>Maintain brand consistency across event touchpoints, adapting our visual language to different contexts, scales, and venue constraints without sacrificing coherence.</li>\n<li>Design environmental graphics, presentations, and interactive elements that communicate complex technical concepts with clarity and engagement.</li>\n<li>Partner with the brand and event marketing teams to ensure creative execution remains aligned with broader strategic direction.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>You may be a good fit if you</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Have extensive experience designing end-to-end event experiences across physical build-outs and digital surfaces, including web, promotional assets, and presentations.</li>\n<li>Have a demonstrated track record of art directing agencies and external vendors — providing clear direction, upholding creative standards, and managing those relationships with confidence.</li>\n<li>Have experience developing strategies for how a brand distinguishes itself in third-party environments — trade shows, industry conferences, enterprise summits — and can speak to work that addressed that challenge effectively.</li>\n<li>Approach booth and spatial design through the lens of attendee experience, with attention not only to aesthetics but to how a space functions for the people moving through it.</li>\n<li>Are a hands-on designer capable of art directing work and sustaining quality across multiple concurrent projects.</li>\n<li>Have a strong eye for brand consistency and the ability to maintain cohesion across diverse applications without producing formulaic work.</li>\n<li>Can translate complex technical subject matter into clear, compelling visual communication.</li>\n<li>Exercise sound judgment in balancing creative ambition with practical constraints in fast-paced environments.</li>\n<li>Thrive in collaborative settings and can manage multiple workstreams with competing timelines while maintaining a high standard of output.</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>The annual compensation range for this role is listed below. </p>\n<p>For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.</p></div><div class=\"title\">Annual Salary:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$260,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;
