(916, 'External Affairs, Brussels', 'Anthropic', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2>About the role</h2>\n<p>We are looking for an experienced EU Policy Analyst to build relationships with external stakeholders and develop policy positions within the EU ecosystem in order to drive progress in AI policy and safety. Working as part of the International Policy team you will help develop policy engagement with the EU institutions, think-tanks, academia and other relevant stakeholders. You will collaborate with policy colleagues on a wide variety of projects: including analysing policy proposals, stakeholder management, policy landscape mapping, drafting submissions for public comment, event planning, and strategic campaign planning to amplify Anthropic\'s policy presence. This role will be crucial in advancing and supporting Anthropic\'s mission within the EU, shaping AI governance to balance safety, innovation, and European competitiveness. </p>\n<h2 class=\"heading\">In this role you will:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Support policy engagement with the EU Commission, parliament, relevant agencies and public sector partners on issues related to government policy and regulatory implications for frontier labs</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Engage key policy stakeholders (e.g., via briefings, consultations, demos, roundtables), in coordination with the wider EMEA policy team</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Partner with the EMEA GTM team to support commercial efforts as appropriate</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Analyze policy proposals, stakeholder management, policy landscape mapping, drafting submissions for public comment, event planning, and strategic campaign planning to amplify Anthropic\'s policy presence.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Help cultivate relationships with key policy and political partners across the EU AI policy ecosystem</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 class=\"heading\">You may be a good fit if you:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Have 5+ years of professional experience working on EU digital policy (individuals with experience in the EU institutions or the Brussels policy ecosystem are desirable);
