(961, 'Industry Principal, Insurance', 'Anthropic', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the role </strong></h2>\n<p>As the Insurance Industry Advisor at Anthropic, you will serve as the technical and strategic face of Claude to the world’s leading insurance carriers, brokers, reinsurers, and insurtech companies. You’ll combine deep insurance domain expertise with technical credibility to help customers envision, architect, and realize transformational AI solutions—while building Anthropic’s reputation as the trusted AI platform for one of the most complex and regulated industries in the world.</p>\n<p>This role sits at the intersection of technical leadership, customer engagement, product strategy, and internal enablement. You’ll work directly with CIOs, CTOs, Chief Underwriting Officers, Chief Claims Officers, and technology leaders at major insurers and brokers to design solutions that address their most critical challenges—from underwriting automation and claims processing to fraud detection and customer experience. Your insights will flow directly to Product and Research, shaping Claude’s roadmap for insurance. Equally important, you’ll enable Anthropic’s GTM teams with deep domain expertise, thought leadership content, and strategic guidance.</p>\n<p>With AI poised to transform insurance operations and the industry seeking partners who understand their unique challenges, you\'ll play a pivotal role in establishing Anthropic as the AI platform of choice for insurers worldwide.</p>\n<h2><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Technical Evangelism &amp; 
INSERT IGNORE INTO `Job` (`id`, `title`, `company`, `description`, `tags`, `location`, `remote`, `jobType`, `sourceApi`, `sourceUrl`, `externalId`, `embedding`, `embeddedAt`, `postedAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `category`) VALUES
(962, 'Infrastructure Engineer, Sandboxing', 'Anthropic', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic is seeking an experienced Infrastructure Engineer to join our Sandboxing team within the Research organization. In this role, you\'ll build and scale the systems that enable researchers to safely execute and experiment with AI-generated code and interactions in isolated environments.</p>\n<p>As our models become more capable, the infrastructure supporting secure execution environments becomes increasingly critical. You\'ll work on distributed systems that must operate reliably at significant scale while maintaining strong security boundaries. Your work will directly support Anthropic\'s mission to develop AI systems that are safe, beneficial, and trustworthy.</p>\n<h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Design, build, and operate distributed backend systems that power secure sandboxed execution environments</li>\n<li>Scale infrastructure to meet growing research and product demands while maintaining reliability and performance</li>\n<li>Implement and maintain serverless architectures and container orchestration systems</li>\n<li>Collaborate with research teams to understand requirements and translate them into robust infrastructure solutions</li>\n<li>Develop monitoring, alerting, and observability systems to ensure operational excellence</li>\n<li>Participate in on-call rotations and incident response to maintain system reliability</li>\n<li>Contribute to infrastructure automation and tooling that improves developer productivity</li>\n<li>Partner with security teams to ensure sandboxing infrastructure maintains appropriate isolation guarantees</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>You may be a good fit if you</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Have 5+ years of experience building and operating backend infrastructure at scale</li>\n<li>Have deep expertise in distributed systems design and implementation</li>\n<li>Have strong operational experience, including debugging complex production issues</li>\n<li>Are proficient with cloud platforms, particularly GCP/GCS (experience with AWS or Azure is also valuable)</li>\n<li>Have experience with containerization technologies (Docker, Kubernetes) and understand their security implications</li>\n<li>Are comfortable working with infrastructure as code and modern DevOps practices</li>\n<li>Have strong programming skills in languages such as Python, Go, or Rust</li>\n<li>Are results-oriented with a bias towards flexibility and impact</li>\n<li>Care about the societal impacts of your work and are motivated by Anthropic\'s mission</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Strong candidates may also have experience with</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Serverless architectures and functions-as-a-service platforms (Cloud Functions, Cloud Run, Lambda)</li>\n<li>Designing and implementing secure multi-tenant systems</li>\n<li>High-performance computing environments or ML infrastructure</li>\n<li>Linux systems internals, including namespaces, cgroups, and seccomp</li>\n<li>Network security and isolation techniques</li>\n<li>Building systems that support research workflows and rapid iteration</li>\n</ul><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>The annual compensation range for this role is listed below. </p>\n<p>For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.</p></div><div class=\"title\">Annual Salary:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$300,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;
INSERT IGNORE INTO `Job` (`id`, `title`, `company`, `description`, `tags`, `location`, `remote`, `jobType`, `sourceApi`, `sourceUrl`, `externalId`, `embedding`, `embeddedAt`, `postedAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `category`) VALUES
(963, 'Integrations Developer', 'Anthropic', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>About the Role</strong></h2>\n<p>As an Integrations Developer at Anthropic, you\'ll be instrumental in powering our go-to-market operations by architecting and implementing scalable integrations that streamline our business systems and automate critical processes. You\'ll work both autonomously and collaboratively to design robust technical solutions that drive our business growth, partnering closely with Data and Engineering teams alongside business stakeholders to translate complex requirements into flexible, secure, and scalable integrations. Your work will directly impact operational efficiency by enabling key functionality such as automating our quote-to-order process, seamlessly integrating business systems, and optimizing our revenue operations - all while shaping our integration architecture to support Anthropic\'s evolution as a fast-growing organization.</p>\n<h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Build Salesforce integrations with downstream systems (Stripe, Forge, and Metronome) in order to automate quote-to-cash processes</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Build and own other business-impacting integrations with Salesforce and other business systems (examples being Hubspot, Iterable, or Clay) in order to automate time-consuming tasks and provide key reporting data or insights to the business</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Implement monitoring and alerting on critical system integrations</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ensure integrations are secure and compliant</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Responsible for maintenance of the integrations and ensuring data quality across systems</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Partner with teams across the company like Data and Engineering to coordinate on upstream and downstream dependencies of the integrations as well as building in line with the company’s engineering best practices and infrastructure</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Collaborate directly with business stakeholders to deeply understand operational workflows and technical requirements</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>You may be a good fit if you:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Have 7+ years of integrations developer experience (both ETL and rETL)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Have experience building integrations with Salesforce and Financial systems (like Stripe, Metronome, or Netsuite)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Have experience automating quote-to-cash functionality</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Advanced integration architecture experience (able to architect a solution from end to end)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Experience with middleware like Mulesoft, Boomi, or Snaplogic</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Experience with Orchestration tools like Airflow and data warehouses like BigQuery or Snowflake</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Software Development best practices with data pipeline monitoring and alerting as well as experience with QA, UAT, and implementing Data Quality checks.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Advanced Data Modeling and SQL expertise</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Working knowledge of scripting languages preferably Python</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Have experience working closely with and implementing solutions for a fast-growing GTM organization</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Possess excellent analytical skills, combined with impeccable business judgment</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Can communicate effectively with management, sales, marketing, vendors and international teams</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Deadline to apply: None. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis.</p><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>The annual compensation range for this role is listed below. </p>\n<p>For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.</p></div><div class=\"title\">Annual Salary:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$190,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;
INSERT IGNORE INTO `Job` (`id`, `title`, `company`, `description`, `tags`, `location`, `remote`, `jobType`, `sourceApi`, `sourceUrl`, `externalId`, `embedding`, `embeddedAt`, `postedAt`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `category`) VALUES
(964, 'Internal Mobility Program Manager', 'Anthropic', '<div class=\"content-intro\"><h2><strong>About Anthropic</strong></h2>\n<p>Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.</p></div><p>We are looking for an Internal Mobility Specialist to join Anthropic\'s People team. In this role, you will build our internal mobility program from the ground up and maintain it over time, creating pathways that help employees grow their careers while meeting the evolving needs of our rapidly scaling organization. You\'ll be the go-to expert for all things related to internal transfers, working at the intersection of People Operations, Recruiting, Finance, and Legal to create seamless experiences for employees exploring new opportunities within Anthropic.</p>\n<p>This is a highly cross-functional role where you\'ll develop strategy while also rolling up your sleeves to handle day-to-day operations. If you thrive in building new programs, enjoy solving complex operational challenges, and care deeply about employee development, this role might be a great fit.</p>\n<h2><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Develop and implement a comprehensive internal mobility program strategy aligned with Anthropic\'s objectives and business needs</li>\n<li>Manage day-to-day operations for internal transfers, including mobility logistics and data processing</li>\n<li>Serve as a trusted resource and guide for employees interested in pursuing new internal opportunities and managers interested in internal talent</li>\n<li>Identify trends in mobility patterns and proactively address process and policy gaps</li>\n<li>Facilitate effective communication and collaboration across stakeholders including employees, managers, People Partners, People Analytics, Recruiting, Immigration, Global Mobility, Finance, Tax, Compensation, and Payroll</li>\n<li>Develop user-friendly documentation, enablement materials, and training resources to educate partner teams on internal mobility programs and processes</li>\n<li>Establish and track key metrics to measure the success and impact of internal mobility initiatives</li>\n<li>Partner with People Analytics and other teams to ensure systems support our internal mobility workflows</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>You may be a good fit if you:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have 7+ years of experience in internal mobility or a related field with exposure to global mobility or workforce planning</li>\n<li>Have experience building or significantly improving programs in a fast-paced, high-growth environment, and can build functional processes without unnecessary red tape</li>\n<li>Are a pragmatic problem-solver who enjoys developing creative solutions to complex operational challenges</li>\n<li>Possess strong communication skills and can build relationships across all levels of an organization</li>\n<li>Thrive in ambiguity and are comfortable creating structure where little exists</li>\n<li>Have a service-oriented mindset and genuinely care about helping employees navigate their career journeys</li>\n<li>Have a strong interest in Anthropic\'s mission and our commitment to developing AI safely and beneficially</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><strong>Strong candidates may also:</strong></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Have experience with global mobility considerations including tax, immigration, and international transfers</li>\n<li>Have worked at a technology company, startup, or similarly dynamic environment</li>\n<li>Have familiarity with HRIS systems and data analysis to track program effectiveness</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p><div class=\"content-pay-transparency\"><div class=\"pay-input\"><div class=\"description\"><p>The annual compensation range for this role is listed below. </p>\n<p>For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (\"OTE\") range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.</p></div><div class=\"title\">Annual Salary:</div><div class=\"pay-range\"><span>$220,000</span><span class=\"divider\">&mdash;
